Welcome back. I’ve reviewed the shared conversation from the previous session—the QuanTM FOAM Arbitrage Casino. The core issue is that the system logs were dumping raw ANSI escape codes (like `[0;32m`) straight into the DOM, making them unreadable. I’ve fixed this by integrating an ANSI-to-HTML converter that transforms those codes into styled `<span>` elements in real time. The logs now display correctly with proper neon coloring (green for success, yellow for warnings, red for errors), bringing that casino-terminal aesthetic to life.

Here’s the corrected and enhanced artifact. You can run it directly to see the improved log rendering, along with the full casino-style arbitrage engine.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
